          "title": "Neunkart",
          "subtitle": "Trick-taking",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "text": "Neunkart is a traditional trick-taking card game using 36-card French-suited pack for 2 or more players. It is also called Fett und Mager and is documented from North German play."
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "text": "Neunkart is treated as a distinct traditional card game because the source identifies its own player count, pack, rank order, and trick-play objective rather than only listing it as a synonym."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "title": "Setup",
          "subtitle": "Table, deck, equipment, and deal",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "text": "2 or more players use the table arrangement described for Neunkart."
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "text": "36-card French-suited pack"
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "text": "36-card French-suited pack, score area, and enough table space for play."
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "text": "Deal 36-card French-suited pack to 2 or more players according to the local rules before trick play begins."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    }
  ]
